{"id": "EUVD-2026-86702", "enisaUuid": "40550b04-b88d-31c5-a519-11e14b598375", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nbpf: zero extend the result of an arena 32-bit cmpxchg\n\nbpf_convert_ctx_accesses() rewrites an atomic on an arena pointer from\nBPF_STX | BPF_ATOMIC to BPF_STX | BPF_PROBE_ATOMIC, and it runs before\nbpf_opt_subreg_zext_lo32_rnd_hi32().\n\nThat pass emits an explicit zero extension for a 32-bit cmpxchg even\nwhen bpf_jit_needs_zext() is false. This is done because on some\narchitectures 32-bit cmpxchg requires explicit zero extension for the\ndst register. E.g. on x86-64 'lock cmpxchg' does not change the %eax\nif comparison is successful, while BPF semantics declare that each\noperation on a 32-bit register zero extends it's upper half.\n\nis_cmpxchg_insn() matches BPF_MODE == BPF_ATOMIC only, so an arena\ncmpxchg misses said zero extension adjustment. This patch adjusts\nis_cmpxchg_insn() to match BPF_PROBE_ATOMIC alongside BPF_ATOMIC.", "datePublished": "2026-09-25T10:23:58", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-21T12:54:16", "baseScore": 0.0, "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/1bb1be18263995b159cf5afad3a05500ba6d2a7b", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/6bb6ae5ab1beffda51dabf41612f501d07f10fc6", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/1c1b476d43a8b6c9bc04600369dd8cc39950d98e", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/4814ed6406f3493bd554ad046da5f7fc04833571"], "aliases": ["GHSA-wmcq-6rpv-m375", "CVE-2026-98049"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.12, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "175d72c5-0c38-3e88-9daf-abbf61906f94", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 0"}, {"id": "52acbf82-9fff-3413-8491-eff9f2e77339", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "6.10"}, {"id": "76ae19ba-12c1-30a0-a03b-cca2e0464d71", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "d503a04f8bc0c75dc9db9452d8cc79d748afb752 <4814ed6406f3493bd554ad046da5f7fc04833571"}, {"id": "78481f35-b18f-36bc-9f2f-77b266aa3195", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.18.57"}, {"id": "82efefe7-fd22-35dc-ac4b-a3e9b90a74d5", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "d503a04f8bc0c75dc9db9452d8cc79d748afb752 <1bb1be18263995b159cf5afad3a05500ba6d2a7b"}, {"id": "9330bc5e-ef1c-3981-a61e-24514401bc00", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "d503a04f8bc0c75dc9db9452d8cc79d748afb752 <6bb6ae5ab1beffda51dabf41612f501d07f10fc6"}, {"id": "addc3640-4d0e-3627-8684-fbb828454ee4", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "d503a04f8bc0c75dc9db9452d8cc79d748afb752 <1c1b476d43a8b6c9bc04600369dd8cc39950d98e"}, {"id": "ce611c93-fa42-35e9-90f4-a55b36e608a2", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.12.114"}, {"id": "d9bdc5fa-e3c1-37ec-92c3-bee02428c6f2", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.3"}, {"id": "e4d7e6f5-cc05-39e6-9d95-d76861aee6bc", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.2.7"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "0372e498-3dfc-3e3e-a59c-3fce160bc3f1", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}], "isExploited": false}